From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: request CPU read access for encoder input
 buffers

EncodeInterface declares the input stream usage as VIDEO_ENCODER only, but
EncodeComponent maps the first input block on the CPU to read its plane
layout, and converts RGB input (screen recording) to NV12 on the CPU for
every frame. Gralloc refuses to lock a buffer that was allocated without
CPU read usage, so with an input surface (camera recording, screenrecord)
the component fails on the first frame and the app gets an error instead
of a recording.

Add C2MemoryUsage::CPU_READ to the input usage. C2StreamUsageTuning holds
C2MemoryUsage bits, which the framework converts to gralloc usage
(CPU_READ becomes SW_READ_OFTEN). A gralloc constant must not be used
here: GRALLOC_USAGE_SW_READ_OFTEN (0x3) reads as CPU_READ | READ_PROTECTED
in C2 terms, so the framework asks gralloc for protected buffers, which
minigbm cannot allocate for RGBA, and screenrecord gets no frames at all.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 components/EncodeInterface.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/EncodeInterface.cpp b/components/EncodeInterface.cpp
index 12152e6..9e66292 100644
--- a/components/EncodeInterface.cpp
+++ b/components/EncodeInterface.cpp
@@ -314,9 +314,16 @@ void EncodeInterface::Initialize(const C2String& name, const SupportedCapabiliti
                     .withConstValue(new C2StreamBufferTypeSetting::input(0u, C2BufferData::GRAPHIC))
                     .build());
 
+    // CPU_READ: EncodeComponent reads the layout of the first input block through a CPU mapping,
+    // and an RGB input (e.g. screen recording) is converted to NV12 on the CPU every frame.
+    // Without it, gralloc refuses to lock input-surface buffers (camera, SurfaceFlinger) and the
+    // component fails on the first frame instead of encoding. This is a C2MemoryUsage value:
+    // use the C2 CPU_READ bit (converted to gralloc SW_READ_OFTEN), not a gralloc constant:
+    // SW_READ_OFTEN (0x3) would read as CPU_READ | READ_PROTECTED and ask for protected buffers.
     addParameter(DefineParam(mInputMemoryUsage, C2_PARAMKEY_INPUT_STREAM_USAGE)
                          .withConstValue(new C2StreamUsageTuning::input(
-                                 0u, static_cast<uint64_t>(BufferUsage::VIDEO_ENCODER)))
+                                 0u, C2MemoryUsage::CPU_READ |
+                                             static_cast<uint64_t>(BufferUsage::VIDEO_ENCODER)))
                          .build());
 
     addParameter(
